\newlabel{fig:synthematic-petersen}{{2}{14}{The synthematic--Petersen dictionary. The five line styles encode the five self-polar triangles as perfect matchings of the six coordinates. For each pair $\{T_i,T_j\}$, their union is an alternating six-cycle: its opposite-edge matching gives a Brianchon point, and its alternating vertex classes give a complementary support pair. Both are represented by the Petersen vertex $ij$; adjacency means that the index pairs are disjoint}{figure.2}{}}
